# Draft knowledge entry: open62541 task and artifact preflight

id: DRAFT-open62541-duplicate-and-artifact-check-1.5.6
trigger_tool: git|conan|registry|preflight
phase: task-initiation|packaging|submission
error_signature: error:system acceleration policy not enabled|packageDetail.*code.*404|same library.*version
severity: 2
category: workflow|conan|registry|deduplication|open62541
match_keywords: open62541, 1.5.6, duplicate branch, duplicate task, CNB registry, packageDetail, code=404, system acceleration policy
title: deduplicate open62541 task lines and inspect CNB package detail instead of SPA HTTP status
root_cause: >
  The Conan client can be blocked by a remote acceleration-policy error, while
  the CNB registry UI is a single-page application that returns HTTP 200 for
  unknown routes. Checking only one signal can cause either a duplicate branch
  or an incorrect version bump.
affected_scope: >
  One-library/one-branch/one-PR HarmonyOS submissions using the CNB Conan
  registry and Git worktrees.
verification_cmd: >
  git branch -r --list '*open62541*';
  test -d archives/o/open62541/1.5.6;
  inspect the exact public registry route for open62541/1.5.6 and require
  packageDetail.data=null with packageDetail.code=404 before treating the
  recipe as unpublished.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: branch-and-package-detail-dedup
rec_description: >
  Reuse the active feature worktree when another remote branch represents the
  same library/version task. Query Conan when permitted; if it is blocked,
  inspect the exact public package-detail payload rather than the SPA HTTP
  status. Keep X.Y.Z for a first publication; use X.Y.Z.N only when the exact
  recipe already exists and the recipe changes.
rec_command: >
  git branch -r --list '*open62541*';
  conan download open62541/1.5.6 -r=ohpcd --only-recipe;
  inspect https://conan.cnb.cool/OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper/Conan/-/registries/open62541/1.5.6
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: one-library-one-branch-preflight
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: public-registry-payload-check
fallback_description: >
  When Conan returns a policy error, do not infer occupancy. Use the public
  route's embedded package detail result and record whether the exact recipe is
  present, absent, or unresolved.
fallback_command: Invoke-WebRequest -Uri <exact-registry-route> -UseBasicParsing
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: registry-evidence-audit
forbid_1_pattern: create a third branch for the same library and version
forbid_1_reason: It violates the one-library/one-branch/one-PR boundary and creates merge ambiguity.
forbid_1_consequence: Duplicate work and competing submissions for one recipe.
forbid_2_pattern: bump the version only because the SPA route returned HTTP 200
forbid_2_reason: The SPA shell returns 200 even when packageDetail.code is 404.
forbid_2_consequence: An unnecessary version suffix permanently changes the intended package coordinate.
principles: task-deduplication, evidence-based-artifact-check, version-discipline
